// S~S  SimpleSal signal starts  S~S

/// [persistence of FSM variables.note]  search in ssTEA source files for a reference to this file.
//
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Finite State Machine (FSM) architectures work well for devices taking action based on Time.
   Any computation answering "how long has it been?" compares the time now to some historical value;
   "time-since-X" is the number of times a unit occured since Time started to run, or was checked.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Traditional, legacy, standard, algorithm midterm, homebrew/DIY, 20th-century FSM solutions are:
        baremetal software in a loop, keeping track of "time-until" and "time-since".  In human
        terms: sample a clock for "how many minutes have occured today?" and then subtract the "how
        many minutes was it when I last sampled?" to find the number of minutes between the samples.
        When the math result of the time-since exceeds the value of time-until, the Event software
        of the App is run, or in ssTEA terms, given Agency by the Agency manager. Software solutions
        Arduino tend to use this method: "please run this software N milliseconds from right now".
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   One view of the limitations of this model is all of the actions are taken based on deltas between
   counters, the concept of "what is the Time Now?".  This Demo App shows the difference between them
   with the BUILTIN LED being managed by a classic Arduino FSM, or, a Time Event running in ssTEA.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   For any FSM to be able to maintain knowledge across time (across function calls, to be specific),
   variables are allocated statically, which really means not on the stack. This may also make data
   globally visible; the key atribute is access at any time (as opposed to only when in a function).
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

